{
  "name": "Track new Google Trends daily and alert on spikes with Apify, Slack and Gmail",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "a1f0c9d2-4b6e-4c1a-9e2f-101a2b3c4d5e",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1220,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 560,
        "height": 1040,
        "content": "## Track new Google Trends daily and alert on spikes\n\n### Who it's for\nMarketing, SEO and content teams, newsrooms and analysts who want a daily, deduplicated trend feed plus an email ping when something big appears.\n\n### How it works\n1. A Schedule Trigger fires once a day and reads your values from the Workflow settings node.\n2. The Apify node runs the [Google Trends Scraper](https://apify.com/orbots/google-trends-scraper) Actor and returns the dataset items. `onlyNew: true` makes it return only trends it has never delivered before: no repeated rows, no double charge for the same trend.\n3. Every new trend (term, estimated search volume, growth, category, active vs ended, duration, link) is appended to a Google Sheet.\n4. A Code node ranks the new trends. If there is anything new, a digest of the top trends goes to Slack.\n5. If any trend crosses your spike threshold (default 500K searches), the workflow also emails you through Gmail.\n6. A separate error branch posts to Slack if a run ever fails.\n\n### Setup steps\n- [ ] Install the verified Apify community node (`@apify/n8n-nodes-apify`) and connect your Apify account\n- [ ] Pick the spreadsheet and sheet in the Google Sheets node\n- [ ] Pick the channel in the two Slack nodes\n- [ ] In Workflow settings, set \"emailTo\" for spike alerts (or leave it empty to turn the email off)\n\n### Cost\nPay-per-event: a typical daily run for one country costs about $0.20, an empty run is free, and the template caps each run at $1.\n\n*Google Trends is a trademark of Google LLC. This template and the underlying Actor are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Google LLC.*"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "b2e1d0c3-5c7f-4d2b-8f30-212b3c4d5e6f",
      "name": "Section 1 fetch",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -620,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 880,
        "height": 414,
        "content": "## 1. Fetch new trends\nThe Workflow settings node holds everything a user edits: countries, trending window, digest size, spike threshold, alert email. The Apify node builds its Actor input from those values and caps each run at 1 USD."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "c3f2e1d4-6d80-4e3c-9041-323c4d5e6f70",
      "name": "Section 2 history",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        320,
        -300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 560,
        "height": 414,
        "content": "## 2. Keep the history\nEvery new trend becomes one row in Google Sheets. Columns map automatically from the item fields. On days with nothing new, no rows are appended and the run is free."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "d5041e26-7f91-4c5d-8152-434d5e6f7081",
      "name": "Section 3 alerts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        320,
        154
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 980,
        "height": 600,
        "content": "## 3. Digest and alerts\nOne Slack message with the top new trends by estimated volume. If any trend beats the spike threshold, Gmail sends an extra alert. Quiet days send nothing and cost nothing."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "e6152f37-8a02-4d6e-9263-545e6f708192",
